# English STT models for contextual-biasing
#
# Format (whitespace separated, '#' starts a comment):
#   <id>  <archive-or-file>  <family>  <tier>  <notes>
#
#   id       : directory name created under models/
#   archive  : asset name in the k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx "asr-models" release
#   family   : transducer | online-transducer | whisper | moonshine
#   tier     : core  -> downloaded by default
#              extra -> downloaded with --all
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BIASING ONLY WORKS ON THE TWO TRANSDUCER FAMILIES.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not because of the encoder. Biasing is a prefix tree over hotword tokens that
# boosts the beam as tokens are emitted, so it needs a decoder that emits tokens
# one at a time under a beam -- i.e. a transducer. Whisper, Moonshine and the
# CTC families have no such hook in sherpa-onnx. Note the pair that proves the
# point: `zipformer-ctc` has the SAME Zipformer encoder and cannot be biased,
# while the NeMo Parakeet below is not a Zipformer at all and can.
#
# A baseline you cannot bias is still worth having -- it answers "is the accent
# problem in the acoustic model or in the language prior?" -- but selecting one
# turns the feature off, and the dashboard says so rather than pretending.
#
# `online-transducer` (streaming) is biasable, but it loads under a different
# recogniser, sees no right context, and the only English export is far over the
# 200 MB device budget. It is a dashboard comparison, not a deployment
# candidate, and ModelRegistry deliberately never picks one as the default.
#
# Both transducer families also need a bpe.vocab, which download_models.sh
# derives (see scripts/bpe_sources.txt). Without it biasing silently degrades
# to nothing.

# --- biasing-capable ------------------------------------------------------
sherpa-onnx-zipformer-small-en-2023-06-26  sherpa-onnx-zipformer-small-en-2023-06-26.tar.bz2  transducer  core   PRIMARY: 27 MB int8, RTF ~0.04, biasing
sherpa-onnx-zipformer-en-2023-06-26        sherpa-onnx-zipformer-en-2023-06-26.tar.bz2        transducer  core   medium zipformer: better WER, ~3x the weights, biasing
sherpa-onnx-zipformer-large-en-2023-06-26  sherpa-onnx-zipformer-large-en-2023-06-26.tar.bz2  transducer  extra  large zipformer: best WER of the family, biasing
sherpa-onnx-nemo-parakeet_tdt_transducer_110m-en-36000-int8  sherpa-onnx-nemo-parakeet_tdt_transducer_110m-en-36000-int8.tar.bz2  transducer  extra  NeMo TDT 110M: strong, heavier, biasing

# --- biasable but streaming: dashboard comparison, NOT for the device -----
# Loads under the online recogniser. Its int8 encoder alone is 127 MB, which is
# over the whole device budget, and a chunk-wise encoder has no right context so
# its WER is worse than the offline models above at any size. Here to make the
# streaming-vs-offline question measurable.
sherpa-onnx-streaming-zipformer-en-2023-02-21  sherpa-onnx-streaming-zipformer-en-2023-02-21.tar.bz2  online-transducer  extra  streaming zipformer: biasable, 128 MB int8, over budget

# --- cannot be biased (baselines only) ------------------------------------
sherpa-onnx-moonshine-tiny-en-quantized-2026-02-27  sherpa-onnx-moonshine-tiny-en-quantized-2026-02-27.tar.bz2  moonshine  core   short-utterance specialist, NO biasing
sherpa-onnx-whisper-base.en                sherpa-onnx-whisper-base.en.tar.bz2                whisper     core   encoder-decoder baseline, NO biasing (no initial_prompt either), 153 MB
sherpa-onnx-whisper-tiny.en                sherpa-onnx-whisper-tiny.en.tar.bz2                whisper     extra  smallest whisper, NO biasing
sherpa-onnx-moonshine-base-en-quantized-2026-02-27  sherpa-onnx-moonshine-base-en-quantized-2026-02-27.tar.bz2  moonshine  extra  strongest non-biasing small option
